    "body": "\n## Problem\n\nRecent two-L40S Modal runs have hit an environment-level NCCL/CUDA failure or\nthe existing no-progress watchdog after capacity was already acquired. The\ncurrent AWS fallback is entered only when Modal cannot acquire capacity, so\nthose runs never exercise the alternate backend. This does not imply that\nevery downstream test failure is caused by Modal.\n\n## Approach\n\nTemporarily route eligible `modal-torch-latest` executions directly through\nthe existing two-GPU AWS controller. This keeps the required job names, trusted\ncheckout and exact candidate SHA handling, test selection, runtime inputs,\ntimeouts, and primary/reconciliation cleanup unchanged. The explicit\ninfrastructure-smoke mode remains available for provider diagnostics.\n\n## Testing\n\nI ran the focused controller/workflow suite because it covers trusted checkout,\ndirect AWS execution, timeout classification, and cleanup behavior.\n\n- `python3 ci/test_torch_latest.py` (49/49 passed)\n- `python3 ci/tests_fetcher.py --base 3b809329fb760de6832d02020e156a9870f5cbdd --explain` (`mode=all`)\n- `pre-commit run --files .github/workflows/modal-torch-latest.yml ci/test_torch_latest.py` (passed)\n- `pre-commit run --all-files` (passed)\n\nA [manual exact-head AWS run](https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/actions/runs/38527813762)\nselected 2,492 `tests/unit/v1` items and exercised two GPUs. It did not pass:\nafter 414 passed and 92 skipped, the unchanged no-progress watchdog terminated\npytest at 20% while\n`TestPerHeadMuonUnderAutoTP::test_the_tags_describe_the_shard_and_not_the_model`\nwas active. No assertion failure was emitted, and workflow cleanup completed.\n\n## Compatibility and disclosure\n\nThis CI-only routing change does not alter DeepSpeed runtime behavior, so ZeRO,\noffload, precision, and parallelism matrix cells are not applicable. Searches\nof open issues and PRs found no existing Torch-latest change that temporarily\nbypasses Modal for direct AWS execution. AI assistance was used to prepare this\nchange; the upstream PR remains a draft for human line-by-line review.\n",
